            <div xml:id="d173">

                <pb facs="0193" n="186" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg186"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/8793: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-16T18:00:00+01:00">July 16, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 16—12:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>479. Your No. 298, July 14, 7 p.m.,<anchor n="24" xml:id="d173-f1"/> referring to
                    the British Ambassador’s conversations with you, Cadogan stated today that he
                    had no additional information and that he felt his Government had done all it
                    could at least for the moment.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
